message: "If you use this code or the derived results in academic work, please cite the manuscript below. The author list must be completed with the real manuscript authors before publication; do not add anyone who is not an author."
title: "Complete genome comparison resolves an att-flanked phage-related element and mixed chromosome states in Enterococcus lactis strains 194 and MGU"
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived results comparing two near-isogenic Enterococcus lactis genome
  deliveries (smbu06 and smbu08): a 38,719-bp differential chromosomal region corresponding
  to an att-flanked phage-related element with a PBSX-family-annotated terminase (present in
  the smbu06 chromosome; the smbu08 assembly retains only the attJ junction sequence and a
  77,437-bp circular component consistent with the excised element), a 128,837-bp plasmid
  shared between the two deliveries, a candidate bacteriocin cassette, and an independent
  Nanopore long-read validation of the attJ junction and of the tandem boundary of the
  circular component. Long-read mappings support the attJ junction state and the
  unit1-to-unit2 boundary, but do not distinguish a tandem dimer from a monomer circle.
  Independent tool cross-validation is included: geNomad (completed; provirus call at the
  element position; no call at the corresponding position of the smbu08 chromosome) and
  PhiSpy (completed; no retained call for the element region).
